###### Open source · Zig · native and web

# Build tools that feel alive.

fizzy is a framework for editors and polished apps: a near-empty host, a stable SDK, and plugins for everything else — tabs, splits, text, images, even a whole pixel-art editor. Native on macOS, Linux and Windows. Live in your browser.

>[]($block.attrs('actions'))
>[Open it in your browser](https://fizzyed.it/app/) [Write a plugin](#write)

[]($section.id('embed'))

This website's own markdown, open in fizzy. It's the real app: drag a tab, open a file.

[]($section.id('framework'))

###### The framework

## A host that owns nothing. Plugins for everything else.

The app is a window, a frame loop, a layout and a document model. Every feature you see — the file tree, the tabs, the text editor — is a plugin registered against the SDK. Plugins never import each other; they meet only there.

- **Regions accept, surfaces offer.** A plugin's view carries keywords saying where it may go, and a region takes what matches. Drag a view somewhere else and the layout remembers.
- **One source, two link modes.** The same plugin compiles into the app — on every target, the web included — or as a library the desktop app loads at runtime. Third-party plugins ship the second way.
- **Copy a layout, don't configure one.** A layout is ordinary Zig, a couple of dozen lines. Use one of the shipped shapes as it is, or copy the closest into your app and change it.

[]($section.id('plugins'))

###### Plugins

## Everything you see is a plugin.

The ones that ship with fizzy are built exactly the way a third-party plugin is, so any of them can be your template.

- **workbench** The file tree and the document panes. Other plugins open and manage files through it without importing it.
- **text** Text and code editing, and the owner of any file nothing else claims.
- **markdown** A live preview for markdown — including this page's.
- **image** A viewer for PNG, JPG, GIF, BMP and TGA, with zoom and pan.
- **archive** Opens a `.zip` as a folder. It's how the window above opened this site.
- **drive** Google Drive as a folder, on the desktop and on the web. From the store.
- **pixi** Pixel art and animation — where fizzy started, now a plugin in the store.

Store plugins live in their own repositories. Tag a release and CI builds it for every desktop target and the web; the registry picks it up, and fizzy installs and updates it in place.

>[]($block.attrs('actions'))
>[Browse the registry](https://github.com/fizzyedit/plugins) [Release CI for your plugin](https://github.com/fizzyedit/plugin-build-action)

[]($section.id('write'))

###### Write a plugin

## One function, one view.

The smallest plugin registers itself and a surface keyworded for the sidebar. Copy it, rename it, `zig build install`, and turn it on in fizzy.

```zig
pub fn register(host: *sdk.Host) !void {
    try host.registerPlugin(&plugin);
    try host.registerSurface(.{
        .id = "hello.greeting",
        .owner = &plugin,
        .title = "Hello",
        .keywords = sdk.keywords.ide.sidebar,
        .draw = draw,
    });
}
```

>[]($block.attrs('actions'))
>[Read the plugin guide](https://github.com/fizzyedit/fizzy/blob/main/docs/PLUGINS.md) [Copy hello-plugin](https://github.com/fizzyedit/fizzy/tree/main/examples/hello-plugin)

[]($section.id('web'))

###### On the web

## The same app, in a tab.

The web build is fizzy compiled to WebAssembly. Nothing to install, and your files stay where they are.

- **Plugins on demand.** Store plugins load beside the app as modules of their own, fetched only when you install one.
- **Folders from anywhere.** Open files from your device, a `.zip` as a folder, or your Google Drive.
- **The desktop app, minus the install.** The same tabs, splits and views, the same plugins.

>[]($block.attrs('actions'))
>[Open fizzy in your browser](https://fizzyed.it/app/)

[]($section.id('status'))

###### Where it stands

## Pre-1.0, and moving fast.

The SDK is versioned, and every plugin is checked against the app's shape when it loads: one built for a different version is turned away rather than crashing.

- [x] A modular core: the app itself owns no features
- [x] The plugin SDK and the plugin store
- [x] The web build, plugins included
- [x] Liquid glass on macOS, frosted glass everywhere
- [x] Pixel art, as the pixi plugin

What comes next is planned in the open, in [GitHub issues](https://github.com/fizzyedit/fizzy/issues).

